sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant WK as apps/worker (yupay_worker.consumer)
    participant D as merchants.webhook_delivery.drain_pending_deliveries
    participant DB as Postgres (the worker's transaction)
    participant OUT as core.outbound.post_json (SSRF-checked)
    participant M as The merchant's server
    participant MAIL as notifications (email)

    Note over WK: this queue's own asyncio task, woken by a NOTIFY on<br/>EITHER channel or by its own poll tick. Its own task because a<br/>gather across both queues returns with the slowest member —<br/>a slow endpoint would become fulfilment's polling period.

    WK->>D: drain_pending_deliveries(db)
    D->>DB: SELECT id, merchant_id FROM merchant_webhook_deliveries<br/>JOIN merchant_webhooks (disabled_at IS NULL)<br/>WHERE status='pending' AND next_attempt_at <= now()<br/>ORDER BY next_attempt_at, created_at, id<br/>LIMIT 20 FOR UPDATE OF deliveries SKIP LOCKED
    Note right of DB: `id` is the tie-break: both timestamps default to<br/>CURRENT_TIMESTAMP = TRANSACTION START, so the paid and<br/>fulfilling rows of one placement are byte-identical in<br/>both. uuid7 encodes enqueue order.

    loop each row, merchant-major (merchants in id order), one SAVEPOINT each
        D->>DB: SELECT disabled_at, secret_enc, secret_nonce
        alt disabled since the claim (admin, or this batch's own auto-disable)
            D-->>WK: skipped, row untouched and still pending
        else enabled
            D->>D: decrypt under PURPOSE_MERCHANT_WEBHOOK, sign<br/>{ts}\n{delivery_id}\n{event_type}\n{sha256(body)}
            D->>DB: attempts_count += 1, status = in_progress
            D->>OUT: POST url (snapshot) + X-Yupay-{Delivery,Event,Timestamp,Signature}
            OUT->>M: TLS to a re-checked, pinned public address

            alt 2xx
                M-->>OUT: 200
                D->>DB: status=delivered, response_code, response_body (clipped 2048)
                D->>DB: hook.failure_streak = 0, last_success_at
            else 408 / 429 / 5xx, or nobody answered (DNS, connect, TLS, timeout, reset)
                D->>DB: status=pending, next_attempt_at = now + backoff<br/>(30s doubling to 1h, Retry-After honoured on 429/503, clamped)
                D->>DB: hook.failure_streak += 1 (hook row locked FOR UPDATE)
            else 4xx / redirect, a RECEIVED refusal (too large, compressed),<br/>or an address WE refused to connect to
                Note right of D: retrying re-delivers, gets the same answer, or<br/>aims at the same refused url snapshot
                D->>DB: status=failed, last_error (clipped 512)
                D->>DB: hook.failure_streak += 1
            else OutboundBrokenError -- our own bug
                D->>DB: status=failed
                Note right of D: the hook is NOT touched: our bug must never<br/>auto-disable a working endpoint
            end

            alt failure_streak reached merchant_webhook_disable_after_failures
                D->>DB: hook.disabled_at = now
                D->>MAIL: schedule_after_commit -> one email per disable,<br/>naming the HOST only (a path can carry a token)
                Note over D,DB: queued rows stay pending — PUT /admin/merchants/{id}/webhook<br/>clears disabled_at + the streak and resumes them
            end
        end
    end

    D-->>WK: rows claimed
    WK->>DB: COMMIT (after every batch), then drain again until a batch is empty
